{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions can contain Solid JSX values or renderer components for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is created in the correct reactive owner and receives its typed context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the recommended JSX component. Give it exactly one table object: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n  {(headerGroup) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n        {(header) => (\n          <th>\n            <Show when={!header.isPlaceholder}>\n              <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n            </Show>\n          </th>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>\n\n<For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n  {(row) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={row.getVisibleCells()}>\n        {(cell) => <td><table.FlexRender cell={cell} /></td>}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The table instance exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":", or you can import the component directly from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-table"},{"type":"text","value":". Its keyed control flow recreates content when a persistent view starts representing a different cell or header. This behavior is important for virtualization and other reused views."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, it chooses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and suppresses grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function renderers are created with Solid's component machinery. The lower-level function does not choose the correct grouped-cell renderer or key the result to a changing table object, so prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" for normal table markup."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers remain the caller's layout decision. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder. Pass footer-group "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<table.FlexRender footer={header} />"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions can contain Solid JSX values or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is created in the correct reactive owner and receives its typed context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended JSX component. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`.\n\n```tsx\n<For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n  {(headerGroup) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n        {(header) => (\n          <th>\n            <Show when={!header.isPlaceholder}>\n              <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n            </Show>\n          </th>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>\n\n<For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n  {(row) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={row.getVisibleCells()}>\n        {(cell) => <td><table.FlexRender cell={cell} /></td>}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>\n```\n\nThe table instance exposes `FlexRender`, or you can import the component directly from `@tanstack/solid-table`. Its keyed control flow recreates content when a persistent view starts representing a different cell or header. This behavior is important for virtualization and other reused views.\n\nFor cells, it chooses `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and suppresses grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nFunction renderers are created with Solid's component machinery. The lower-level function does not choose the correct grouped-cell renderer or key the result to a changing table object, so prefer `FlexRender` for normal table markup.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the caller's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder. Pass footer-group `Header` objects with `<table.FlexRender footer={header} />`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Solid) Guide\n---\n\nColumn definitions can contain Solid JSX values or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is created in the correct reactive owner and receives its typed context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended JSX component. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`.\n\n```tsx\n<For each={table.getHeaderGroups()}>\n  {(headerGroup) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={headerGroup.headers}>\n        {(header) => (\n          <th>\n            <Show when={!header.isPlaceholder}>\n              <table.FlexRender header={header} />\n            </Show>\n          </th>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>\n\n<For each={table.getRowModel().rows}>\n  {(row) => (\n    <tr>\n      <For each={row.getVisibleCells()}>\n        {(cell) => <td><table.FlexRender cell={cell} /></td>}\n      </For>\n    </tr>\n  )}\n</For>\n```\n\nThe table instance exposes `FlexRender`, or you can import the component directly from `@tanstack/solid-table`. Its keyed control flow recreates content when a persistent view starts representing a different cell or header. This behavior is important for virtualization and other reused views.\n\nFor cells, it chooses `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and suppresses grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable value and context:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nFunction renderers are created with Solid's component machinery. The lower-level function does not choose the correct grouped-cell renderer or key the result to a changing table object, so prefer `FlexRender` for normal table markup.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the caller's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders that placeholder. Pass footer-group `Header` objects with `<table.FlexRender footer={header} />`.\n"}
